,title,link,text,language,family
0,Yana language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yana_language,"The Yana language (also Yanan) is an extinct language that was formerly spoken by the Yana people, who lived in north-central California between the Feather and Pit rivers in what is now the Shasta and Tehama counties.",Yana,Language isolate
1,Yahi dialect - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yahi_dialect,"Yahi was a dialect of the extinct Yana language that was spoken in the upper Sacramento Valley area, roughly in the area between Mill Creek and Deer Creek. It is one of the southern dialects of Yana, which is a language isolate, though with possible connections to Hokan. Yana is known as having been the language of Ishi, the last surviving Yana Indian, who worked with anthropologists to make a ...",Yana,Language isolate
2,Yana language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Yana_language,"The Yana language is an extinct Indigenous language of California, formerly spoken by the Yana people in the hills and canyons along the eastern edge of the Sacramento Valley, between the Pit River to the north and the Feather River to the south. [1] It featured three main dialects—Northern Yana, Central Yana, and Southern Yana (also known as Yahi, the southernmost)—each associated with ...",Yana,Language isolate
3,Yana - California Language Archive,https://cla.berkeley.edu/languages/yana.html,"The Southern Yana were also called the Yahi. In pre-contact times, there were likely around 1,500 speakers (Kroeber 1925). In the 21st century, there are no first-language speakers (Golla 2011). Yana is an isolate within the hypothesized Hokan language family.",Yana,Language isolate
4,Isolate by Yana Afanaseva | Mixcloud,https://www.mixcloud.com/yana-afanaseva/isolate/,Listen to Isolate by Yana Afanaseva for free. Follow Yana Afanaseva to never miss another show.,Yana,Language isolate
5,Yana language - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Yanan_language,"Classification Yana is often classified in the Hokan superstock. Sapir suggested a grouping of Yana within a Northern Hokan sub-family with Karuk, Chimariko, Shastan, Palaihnihan, and Pomoan. Contemporary linguists generally consider Yana to be a language isolate. [5][6]",Yana,Language isolate
6,Yana language - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Yahi_language,"Yana is often classified in the Hokan superstock. Sapir suggested a grouping of Yana within a Northern Hokan sub-family with Karuk, Chimariko, Shastan, Palaihnihan, and Pomoan. Contemporary linguists generally consider Yana to be a language isolate. [5][6] Yana employs 22 consonants and 5 vowels.",Yana,Language isolate
7,Language Isolates be like - YouTube,https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=2cKpksz_2Q8,"A Language isolate can be defined as a language with no traceable relationship to any other language. Most modern languages share similar characteristics with others, but there are some that are ...",Yana,Language isolate
8,Sounds - Ishi's Echo,https://ishisecho.humspace.ucla.edu/sounds/,"The rhythmic patterns may have mimicked natural sounds or movements associated with hunting. Language Notes: The vocal techniques in this recording demonstrate how Yahi music incorporated sounds from the natural environment, possibly imitating animal calls or environmental sounds relevant to hunting.",Yana,Language isolate
9,PDF Cylinder recordings of Ishi - Library of Congress,https://www.loc.gov/static/programs/national-recording-preservation-board/documents/IshiCylinderRecordings.pdf,"Unfortunately, many of the texts remain untranslated. As the only sound recordings of the music and speech of the southern Yana peoples, this set of cylinders--still at the Hearst Museum--has been repeatedly transferred and restored over the past century.",Yana,Language isolate
